{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling: power mode 0 is the condition for a gate, from AC or battery.\nThis act revises f27885cc.\n\nf27885cc held gates to AC because the battery profile set power mode\n1, Low Power Mode, and Native cases timed out. That cause is gone.\n\nRead at 08:29 EST on 14 November:\n\n- `pmset -g custom` shows `powermode 0` under \"Battery Power\" and\n  under \"AC Power\".\n- `pmset -g` shows `powermode 0`. powerd, Amphetamine and caffeinate\n  prevent sleep.\n- The machine draws from the battery since 08:06:36. The charge is\n  97 %.\n- On 13 November the charge fell from 100 % at 18:05 to 28 % at\n  22:39 under lane load with no gate. That is about 16 % each hour.\n\nThe rule from now:\n\n1. A gate or an evidence interval starts when `pmset -g` reads\n   `powermode 0`. The power source can be AC or the battery.\n2. On battery, the charge at START is 50 % or more. Below 50 %, no\n   gate and no interval starts.\n3. The START act and the END act each state the power source, the\n   charge and the power mode.\n4. Each power sample of the run reads power mode 0. One sample with\n   power mode 1 fails the interval. A change of power source during\n   the run does not fail it.\n5. `pmset -g log` shows no sleep between START and END, as before.\n6. If a gate on battery fails on a timeout, report the case, the\n   elapsed time and the power readings. Then gates wait for AC until\n   I rule again. Do not change a test or a timeout.\n\nEach supervisor check that requires AC changes to this condition:\npower mode 0, and AC or a charge of 50 % or more. Make that one\nchange in the R2 Grow focused plan and in the R2 Grow gate plan now,\nand freeze them again. The NF-5 plan and each later plan take the\nsame change before their turn. The changed check accepts AC, so one\nchange serves both sources.\n\nThe queue of b12acd6c stands. The R2 Grow focused interval can start\nwhen its plan is ready.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}